// Example 3: Side-effect only call (no return statement)
//
// log has no return statement, so it implicitly returns nil.
// The call is in statement position.
//
// Discussion: is this call "a statement" because we only care about the
// effect (printing)? Or is it still an expression (it evaluates to nil)
// that happens to be discarded?
//
// Compare with: what's the difference between a statement and an
// expression used for effect only?

fun log(msg) {
  print("[LOG] " + msg);
}

log("start");   // effect only - does anything about this line need the value?
